# Call-site ledger of pymysql at c990e86083c26493f3285b1e047902994c4b1811.
# Decide every `undecided` line; see macro-benchmark/README.md.
#
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md; pymysql.md
# shows how this ledger applies them. pymysql 1.2.3 declares Python >= 3.9 and
# the implementations CPython and PyPy (pyproject.toml classifiers,
# docs/source/user/installation.rst). cryptography and PyNaCl are optional
# extras that the test environment does not install: their calls are named as
# missing modules. The module flags DEBUG (connections, protocol, _auth) are
# False and nothing in the package, its tests or its documentation sets them
# (tests/test_auth.py:7-8 only has them commented out), so the `if DEBUG:`
# branches do not run (pymysql.md, judgement J1).
default reject pymysql.protocol.OKPacketWrapper.__getattr__: the receiver of this attribute load is not an OKPacketWrapper, or the attribute is one that OKPacketWrapper.__init__ sets on the instance (affected_rows, insert_id, server_status, warning_count, message, has_next, packet); the only load that reaches __getattr__ is self.read_struct in OKPacketWrapper.__init__ (protocol.py:299), which accepts it
default reject pymysql.protocol.EOFPacketWrapper.__getattr__: the receiver of this attribute load is not an EOFPacketWrapper, or the attribute is one that EOFPacketWrapper.__init__ sets on the instance (packet, warning_count, server_status, has_next); the package reads only those from its EOFPacketWrapper objects (connections.py:1366-1367), and no wrapper reaches a client
default reject pymysql.protocol.LoadLocalPacketWrapper.__getattr__: the receiver of this attribute load is not a LoadLocalPacketWrapper, or the attribute is one that LoadLocalPacketWrapper.__init__ sets on the instance (packet, filename); the package reads only filename (connections.py:1343), and no wrapper reaches a client
default reject pymysql.DBAPISet.__eq__: no DBAPISet takes part in this comparison, `in` test or key lookup; the package never compares, hashes or stores its DBAPISet constants (STRING, BINARY, ...), only clients do; in DBAPISet's own `in` tests, only the lookup of __ne__ (__init__.py:87:26), whose other can be a DBAPISet, can meet a DBAPISet.__eq__, and it accepts it (judgement J12); in __eq__'s lookup (93:26) other is not a frozenset
default reject pymysql.DBAPISet.__hash__: no DBAPISet is hashed at this site (see the default for DBAPISet.__eq__); DBAPISet.__ne__ accepts it at its `in` test (__init__.py:87), where a client compares two DBAPISets
default reject pymysql.DBAPISet.__ne__: no DBAPISet is the left operand of this comparison (see the default for DBAPISet.__eq__)
default reject pymysql.charset.Charset.__repr__: no Charset is formatted, converted to str or repr at this site; the package only reads id, name, collation, is_default, encoding and is_binary of its Charset objects
default reject pymysql.protocol.FieldDescriptorPacket.__str__: no FieldDescriptorPacket is formatted or converted to str at this site; the one format of a field (connections.py:1484) is under `if DEBUG:`, which does not run (judgement J1)
default reject pymysql.cursors.Cursor.__iter__: no cursor is iterated or unpacked at this site; the package never iterates one of its cursors (the iteration of SSCursor.fetchall goes over iter(self.fetchone, None), a callable iterator)
default reject pymysql.cursors.Cursor.__next__: no cursor is iterated or unpacked at this site (see the default for Cursor.__iter__)
